{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791103096,"nonce":"NeECY+5DrScjCLt90xbWxfQd2yg=","title":"Text and images under a square clip inside a squircle clip draw at half coverage","message":"An accordion's open content (overflow: hidden, inside the accordion's overflow: hidden squircle panel) drew its text at 50% alpha in the top half of the content and fully in the bottom half.\n\nCause: clipping() folds nested clips into one rect with per-corner radii, keeping a corner's radius only where the intersection still reaches into the source clip's rounded corner, but takes the corner shape n from the innermost rounded clip regardless. Corners whose radius drops to 0 keep the squircle n. In sdShapedRect a superellipse of radius 0 returns 0 everywhere, so d = max(box, 0) = 0 inside, and clipCoverage gives 0.5. The box shader passes its own n, so fills were unaffected; text, images, shadows and backdrops take the record's clip n and were.\n\nReproducer: an image or text inside a 16x16 overflow-clip box centred in a 56x56 overflow-clip box with radius 18, corner-shape squircle (tests/fixtures/render/Pixels.hx \"nested clips\"). Before: [231,128,151] where red was drawn. After: [255,0,0].\n\nFix: sdShapedRect returns the sharp box for a corner of no radius, whatever its shape.","files":null}]}